cusing on methods and experiments. Structure your output as:\n\n1. **Summary** (2-3 sentences)\n2. **Strengths** (numbered list, be specific about what works well methodologically)\n3. **Weaknesses** (numbered list, be specific and cite tables/sections)\n4. **Questions for Authors** (numbered)\n5. **Missing Experiments or Analyses**\n6. **Score** (1-6) with one-line justification\n7. **Confidence** (1-5: 1=low, 5=expert)\n\nBe rigorous. A top venue expects strong methodology. Focus on: experimental design validity, statistical rigor, confound control, generalizability of findings, adequacy of the factorial design, and whether the results support the claims.","uuid":"dbecc233-8b17-42d5-a9c5-166e3381434f","session_id":"56dac4e5-2ce5-4fbd-b248-0bfac99e4894"}
